## Installation

### macOS / Linux

**Homebrew (recommended on macOS):**

```bash
brew install {{.HomebrewTap}}/{{.BinaryName}}
```

**Shell script:**

```bash
curl -fsSL https://{{.Domain}}/cli/install.sh | sh
```

### Windows

**PowerShell:**

```powershell
irm https://{{.Domain}}/cli/install.ps1 | iex
```

**Command Prompt (CMD):**

```cmd
curl -fsSL https://{{.Domain}}/cli/install.cmd -o install.cmd && install.cmd
```

### Verify installation

```bash
{{.BinaryName}} --help
```

## Prerequisites (development)

- [Go](https://go.dev/dl/) {{.GoVersion}}+
- Access to a {{.PrettyName}} organization

## Development

```bash
git clone https://{{.ModulePath}}.git
cd {{.RepoName}}
bin/setup
```

This installs Go dependencies, golangci-lint, configures git hooks, and builds the binary.

### Make targets

```bash
make build          # Builds ./{{.BinaryName}}
make test           # Run tests
make lint           # golangci-lint
make fmt            # gofmt -w
make vet            # go vet
make check          # fmt + vet + test
make install        # Installs to /usr/local/bin
make clean          # Remove built binary
```

### Pointing to a local or staging server

Set `{{.EnvVar}}` to override the default `https://<subdomain>.{{.Domain}}`:

```bash
export {{.EnvVar}}=http://acme.lvh.me:8980
{{.BinaryName}} login --subdomain acme
```

## Global flags

Every command accepts:

| Flag | Description |
|---|---|
| `--subdomain <name>` | Which logged-in subdomain to use (required when multiple are logged in). |
| `--json` | Force JSON envelope output. |
| `--quiet` | Emit raw data only. Action commands print just the identifier; `delete` prints `success`. |
| `--toon` | TOON (Token-Optimized Output Notation) — compact format for LLMs. |

